# What are their babies called?
subtitle: "Joey, cygnet, leveret, elver: match four animals to the names of their young, and meet the best baby name of all."

## What are their babies called?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: am
      title: Echidnas; Macquarie Dictionary entry 'puggle'
      authors: Australian Museum
      year: 2023
      finding: a baby echidna is called a puggle (the word may have begun as a soft-toy name); a newborn kangaroo joey is about the size of a jelly bean

    cards babies hidden true
        * "Kangaroo" icon.of kangaroo icon.set twemoji match Joey
        * "Swan" icon.of swan icon.set twemoji match Cygnet
        * "Hare" icon.of rabbit icon.set twemoji match Leveret
        * "Eel" icon ["eel","fish"] match Elver
    text ech "echidna's baby" #b5482e x 500 y 600 font_size 44 hidden true
    text puggle "Puggle" #b5482e cites ["am"] x 760 y 420 font_size 84 hidden true
    icon ech_big size 260 x 330 y 400 or ["hedgehog","porcupine"] icon_look picture of echidna hidden true
    icon ech_baby size 90 x 560 y 330 or ["hedgehog","porcupine"] icon_look picture of echidna hidden true

    card title "What are their babies called?"

What do you call a baby kangaroo? Or a baby swan? Many animals' young have names of their own.
    draw babies

    ask "Match each animal to the name of its young: drag from one card to its partner." on babies store m feedback.style warm feedback.perfect "Were you raised by a zookeeper?" feedback.good "The nursery is in safe hands." feedback.poor "Most people only know the joey." feedback.none "The baby names got away this time. Never mind."
        right: All four pairs right.
        wrong: {m} right. Here are the true pairs.

A baby kangaroo is a joey, born about the size of a jelly bean, and raised in its mother's pouch.
    highlight babies_1 babies_m_1

A young swan is a cygnet, from cygnus, the Latin for swan.
    highlight babies_2 babies_m_2

A young hare is a leveret, from the old French word for a hare.
    highlight babies_3 babies_m_3

And a young eel is an elver, swimming in from the sea after a journey of thousands of kilometres.
    highlight babies_4 babies_m_4

    erase babies

But the best name of all belongs to the echid (@draw ech ech_big ech_baby puggle@)na, the spiny egg-laying mammal of Australia. Its baby is a puggle.

A puggle hatches from an egg about the size of a grape: tiny, pink, and with no spines yet.
    highlight ech_baby puggle
